content.text:
You're already displaying series names at the right edge via `endLabel`. To also show the rank value on every data point, add a `label` block to the series definition inside `generateSeriesList`.

```js
const series = {
  name,
  symbolSize: 20,
  type: 'line',
  smooth: true,
  emphasis: {
    focus: 'series'
  },
  label: {
    show: true,
    position: 'inside',
    formatter: '{c}',
    fontSize: 10,
    color: '#fff'
  },
  endLabel: {
    show: true,
    formatter: '{a}',
    distance: 20
  },
  lineStyle: {
    width: 4
  },
  data
};
```

Since `symbolSize` is 20, `position: 'inside'` puts the rank number right in the circle, which reads well for a bump chart. If you'd rather keep the symbols clean, use `position: 'top'` with `distance: 8` and drop the white color so labels inherit the series color.

A couple of variants depending on what you meant by "label":

- **Name plus rank at the end of each line**: change the `endLabel.formatter` to a function, `formatter: (params) => `${params.seriesName} (#${params.value})``.
- **Labels only on the first and last year**, to reduce clutter: keep `label.show: false` on the series and instead pass per-point objects in `data`, e.g. `{ value: rank, label: { show: true } }` for the indices you want.

One thing to watch: with nine series crossing each other, always-on labels can overlap. `labelLayout: { hideOverlap: true }` on the series suppresses colliding labels automatically.

I need to add label configuration to display the rank values on each data point in the bump chart, showing them above the symbols using the value formatter.

Here's the full example with the rank label rendered on every point of every series. Since each year has a unique rank per line, the labels never collide, so nothing needs to be suppressed.

```js
const names = [
  'Orange',
  'Tomato',
  'Apple',
  'Sakana',
  'Banana',
  'Iwashi',
  'Snappy Fish',
  'Lemon',
  'Pasta'
];
const years = ['2001', '2002', '2003', '2004', '2005', '2006'];
const shuffle = (array) => {
  let currentIndex = array.length;
  let randomIndex = 0;
  while (currentIndex > 0) {
    randomIndex = Math.floor(Math.random() * currentIndex);
    currentIndex--;
    [array[currentIndex], array[randomIndex]] = [
      array[randomIndex],
      array[currentIndex]
    ];
  }
  return array;
};
const generateRankingData = () => {
  const map = new Map();
  const defaultRanking = Array.from({ length: names.length }, (_, i) => i + 1);
  for (const _ of years) {
    const shuffleArray = shuffle(defaultRanking);
    names.forEach((name, i) => {
      map.set(name, (map.get(name) || []).concat(shuffleArray[i]));
    });
  }
  return map;
};
const generateSeriesList = () => {
  const seriesList = [];
  const rankingMap = generateRankingData();
  rankingMap.forEach((data, name) => {
    const series = {
      name,
      symbolSize: 20,
      type: 'line',
      smooth: true,
      emphasis: {
        focus: 'series'
      },
      label: {
        show: true,
        position: 'inside',
        formatter: '{c}',
        fontSize: 10,
        fontWeight: 'bold',
        color: '#fff'
      },
      labelLayout: {
        hideOverlap: false
      },
      endLabel: {
        show: true,
        formatter: '{a}',
        distance: 20
      },
      lineStyle: {
        width: 4
      },
      data
    };
    seriesList.push(series);
  });
  return seriesList;
};
option = {
  title: {
    text: 'Bump Chart (Ranking)'
  },
  tooltip: {
    trigger: 'item'
  },
  grid: {
    left: 30,
    right: 110,
    bottom: 30,
    containLabel: true
  },
  toolbox: {
    feature: {
      saveAsImage: {}
    }
  },
  xAxis: {
    type: 'category',
    splitLine: {
      show: true
    },
    axisLabel: {
      margin: 30,
      fontSize: 16
    },
    boundaryGap: false,
    data: years
  },
  yAxis: {
    type: 'value',
    axisLabel: {
      margin: 30,
      fontSize: 16,
      formatter: '#{value}'
    },
    inverse: true,
    interval: 1,
    min: 1,
    max: names.length
  },
  series: generateSeriesList()
};
```

The only changes are the `label` and `labelLayout` blocks in `generateSeriesList`. `labelLayout: { hideOverlap: false }` is the default, but stating it explicitly guarantees ECharts won't drop any label if you later increase the font size or switch to `position: 'top'`.

If you also want the series name repeated at each point rather than only at the line's end, change the formatter to `'{a} #{c}'` and move the label outside the symbol with `position: 'top'` and `color: 'inherit'` — though with nine lines and six years that's 54 labels, which will get crowded.

The user wants to see all labels displayed on every data point across all series without any overlaps being hidden, so I need to provide the complete modified example code with label configurations that ensure visibility on each point.
